  [SIZE=4]Missing/Incorrect entries[/SIZE]
If you are here because you want to report an error in the data, please check  [URL="https://www.esoui.com/portal.php?&id=177&pageid=63"]here[/URL] on how to get item links.
Feel free to send us a message (here or in game) with the item info for timely updates!

[SIZE=5][COLOR=PaleGreen]Features[/COLOR]:[/SIZE] 
[SIZE=3]Check the screenshots![/SIZE][LIST]
[*]    [SIZE=4]User-Interface[/SIZE]: [I]toggleable either via [B]keybind[/B] or via [B]slash command[/B][/I][LIST]
[*][I]/fur for main window[/I]
[*][I]/furc for settings[/I][/LIST] 
[*]    [SIZE=3][URL="https://www.esoui.com/downloads/info1865-FurnitureShoppingListpatched.html"]FurnitureShoppingList[/URL][/SIZE]: [I]Fully integrated[/I]
[*]    [SIZE=3]Compact/Full view[/SIZE]:    [I]Check the +/- button[/I]
[*]    [SIZE=3]Item database[/SIZE]: [I]Holds a list of all available furniture blueprints (source: I datamined them myself! ^_^)        [/I]
[*]    [SIZE=3]Filters[/SIZE]: [I]All filters are additive - check screenshots[/I][LIST]
[*] crafting station
[*] crafting knowledge
[*] item source
[*] quality
[*] game version
[*] item name
[*] multi-source selection via right-clicking[/LIST] 
[*]    [SIZE=3]Category filters[/SIZE] [I]Filters furnishings of selected sources or filters by category (lighting, structure, etc.)[/I]
[*]    [SIZE=3]Post to chat [/SIZE] [I]Print the recipe (if known) or the material list to chat from an item link or the Interface (2nd and 3rd screenshots)[/I]
[*]    [SIZE=3]Lists[/SIZE] [I]Create multiple editable lists which are fully integrated with FurnitureShoppingList and LFC's external webui![/I]
[*]    [SIZE=3]Responsive developer[/SIZE] [I]Found something that's not in the catalogue? Tell us where you got it, send an item link, and in it goes![/I][/LIST][SIZE=5][COLOR=DarkRed]Not possible[/COLOR]:[/SIZE][LIST]
[*] Preview: I can't let you preview things from Furniture Catalogue. Scroll down for the long explanation.
[*] Crown Store: I can't access Crown Store tooltips. If you have a crown store item, please send us the link and price![/LIST][COLOR=Wheat][SIZE=4]Why should I use this instead of CraftStore?[/SIZE][/COLOR]
You probably shouldn't - this AddOn has a different purpose. I wrote FurnitureCatalogue to help me with furnishing my homes - I wanted to know [U]what's out there[/U] and [U]how I can get it[/U].

[COLOR=Green][SIZE=5]Donations welcome![/SIZE][/COLOR]
Writing this AddOn was [B]a lot[/B] of work. Almost all the included data files are generated by hand. I have literally spent hours just standing in front of furniture merchants, checking item conditions and putting things into files.
By careful estimate I've spent 30+ hours on FurC since Morrowind hit PTS - the initial release ate a week of vacation turned to pretty much nonstop coding. 
[B]@WolfStar07 has[/B][B] taken over updating since manavortex no longer plays ESO, so if you want to give back, feel free to donate to @WolfStar07, both on NA and EU! [/B]

[SIZE=5][COLOR=Yellow]Possible issues[/COLOR][/SIZE] 

[SIZE=4]How do I manage my crafter's knowledge?[/SIZE]
You need LibCharacterKnowledge (LCK) for chars to appear. Manage your tracked chars in LCK settings (they have to be tracked and they have to track furnishing plans of any quality to appear).

[SIZE=4]Something else is broken![/SIZE][LIST=1]
[*]Disable AddOns that overwrite ESO functions or libraries
[*]Reset the furniture catalogue database by right or middle-clicking the refresh button
[*]Wipe the saved variables - you can do that from the AddOn menu via "Reset to default".
[*]Do a clean install of the AddOn to make sure no outdated files are left
[*]Get in touch with us with a description of the bug, in the [URL="https://www.esoui.com/downloads/info1617-FurnitureCatalogue.html#comments"]forums[/URL] or on [URL="https://github.com/manavortex/FurnitureCatalogue/issues"]GitHub[/URL]:[LIST]
[*]Where exactly does it occur? (FurnitureCatalogue window, when right-clicking an item link...)
[*]What is affected? (item links, posting to chat, exporting...)
[*]What do we have to do to reproduce this bug?[/LIST] [/LIST][I]Big thanks to our fellow developers for being so awesome and helping me out so much![/I]

[SIZE=5][COLOR=Wheat]The long version about the preview[/COLOR][/SIZE]
I have talked to Chip Hilseberg (may his code never bug) about this, and he was quite clear - ZOS doesn't want us to preview items from the item links because of datamining etc. A function to preview items that we can craft may come eventually, but that will only help you while logged in on your crafter. 

[SIZE=4]Why can't you make it work like FurniturePreview?[/SIZE]
There is an API function that lets you preview something that is in a bag (a vendor is a bag too) or a guild store. In theory I could add preview functions from Furniture Catalogue for items that are in your inventory, but that would require yet another loop and have a negative impact on performance. (Again.) Just use FurniturePreview for those, please.

